# Images & Assets

## next/image

- Always use `next/image`. Never `<img>` except inside inline SVG `<svg>` content.
- `src` must come from either:
  - `public/figma/*` (allowed via `images.localPatterns` `/figma/**` in `next.config.ts`)
  - Payload Media via `/api/media/file/**`
- Provide `alt`. Decorative imagery uses `alt=""` + `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Provide an honest `sizes` prop on `fill` images, not `310px` everywhere. Example: `(min-width: 1536px) 348px, (min-width: 768px) 316px, 281px`.
- For SVG icons rendered as `<Image src="/figma/foo.svg" />` use explicit `width` / `height`; for inline color-controllable icons inline the SVG and use `currentColor`.

## Figma Assets

- Download from `https://www.figma.com/api/mcp/asset/...` URLs to `public/figma/`. These URLs expire in 7 days; the file on disk is the source of truth.
- Name files in kebab-case with a section prefix: `offer-session-kobieca.png`, `intro-quote-mark.svg`, `home-hero-bg.png`.
- Verify the actual MIME after download (`file public/figma/<name>`). Figma sometimes returns PNG bytes for a `.jpg` URL; rename to match real format.
- Delete unused assets when removing a section; do not leave orphaned PNG/SVGs in `public/figma/`.

## When CMS-driven

Once a section is migrated to a Payload block, the `imageSrc` must come from a Media relation. The `public/figma/*` versions then become **fallbacks** for the static seed only (see `cms-readiness.mdc`).
